b.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-beets/compare/nightly-ad27129f-ls20...nightly-718dc3ae-ls21","upstream":"smartplaylist: accept library for relative_to (#7175)\n\n## Description\n\nFixes #5348.\nproposed solution: The playlist plugin accepts library for relative_to\nhowever smartplaylist treated every value as a path. Setting\nrelative_to: library made paths relative to a folder named library in\nthe current directory, rather than to the music library. This makes\nsmartplaylist accept library for both the relative_to option and the\nrelative-to flag. Paths are then made relative to the library directory,\nso the two plugins can be used together without a hardcoded path.\n\n## To Do\n\n<!--\n- If you believe one of below checkpoints is not required for the change\nyou\nare submitting, cross it out and check the box nonetheless to let us\nknow.\n  For example: - [x] ~Changelog~\n- Regarding the changelog, often it makes sense to add your entry only\nonce\nreviewing is finished. That way you might prevent conflicts from other\nPR's in\nthat file, as well as keep the chance high your description fits with\nthe\n  latest revision of your feature/fix.\n- Regarding documentation, bugfixes often don't require additions to the\ndocs.\n- Please remove the descriptive sentences in braces from the enumeration\nbelow,\n  which helps to unclutter your PR description.\n-->\n\n- [ x] Documentation. (If you've added a new command-line flag, for\nexample, find the appropriate page under `docs/` to describe it.)\n- [x ] Changelog. (Add an entry to `docs/changelog.rst` to the bottom of\none of the lists near the top of the document.)\n- [ x] Tests. (Very much encouraged but not strictly required.)","upstream_url":"https://github.com/beetbox/beets/commit/718dc3ae6a75f81bcded19cc31c298289dc5889d"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","PS1=$(whoami)@$(hostname):$(pwd)\\$ ","HOME=/config","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_